{"title":"2018 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part D","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.5_(Modular_Arithmetic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.5 (Modular Arithmetic)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2018 CIMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <i>range</i> of a list of numbers is the difference between the largest number and the smallest number in the list. For example, the range of the list <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e7f8bc14cdd0631cafcfbbc1b5eff7c66c6b959.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 5, 1, 6, 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/d/74dbf5a4d426fb8bb63d88ab4f21b351d2ee670c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 - 1 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_D&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The list <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/c/e5c1c9c5036ab328ac9dae49df704b943d89f68d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 2x^{2}, 6 + 4x^{2}, 6, 6 + 5x^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"210\" height=\"20\" /> has a range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Determine the two possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_D&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are positive, we can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/1/e618f4331335d45c3423625dda64793a2600bd18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax + by$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> must increase as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> increase and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/1/e618f4331335d45c3423625dda64793a2600bd18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax + by$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> is positive since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are both positive, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/a/16ac88dd5af044d10a9c0e3fddbbe05f95c9a91d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ax$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" /> is positive and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9ed8bd877353f4f9c1305efbcbebcea0ec506f74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$by$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"16\" /> is positive. Thus, the smallest number in the list is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the largest number in the list is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/1/8614d3c64231e5984953424133c0605f8f000df9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x + 3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />. \n</p><p>This means that the range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is also equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/5/7f5a95d92aecc51c27f7a3bf4055bef9d463750b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x + 3y - 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" />, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/d/efd5af5222f3d671e7d292d33599ff82e2edf247.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x + 3y = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/2/cf274af4af8c0546eca132629e3e6dfa4bc4a944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x \\geq 5 \\times 4 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" />, which would make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/89385605cebfe24cd5d7a9402a2908b64a012fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> negative and also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> would be negative. This means that we can just plug-in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2effc7979b1c93e59356b73253d75e2740b33105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690ef55a607beaf2389d1ee102df817721bc2392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> until we find a solution:\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/b/aabc36e6e5baa8665c5f01e56b540d3d1693b06e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 1 + 3y = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b9166eb4d565a557630a225955e6e5a246aa1d08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y + 5 = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/914c21c4e2b04b90cb646fa96907b342794767f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y = 19 - 5 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must be an integer, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/89385605cebfe24cd5d7a9402a2908b64a012fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> cannot be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <i>not</i> a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a4ecb65de08c1bf479a1947129ae25b83e78bd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\neq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2effc7979b1c93e59356b73253d75e2740b33105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, then:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/3/f6371dc8548242509ff383f44f2c507aa968d80d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 2 + 3y = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/1/f11fb97df4201c21973ab5ead56ce73e5ab1dc93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y + 10 = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/4/a544fc238093b398d4ae18b830bfcfbf8345fcef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y = 19 - 10 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf4970651363deb838295ba64962968af217af5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{9}{3} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>This works out since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/89385605cebfe24cd5d7a9402a2908b64a012fa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> here, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b124361978352af059e12c33e0b92950ae1c850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x = 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"57\" height=\"25\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd92814176db02f14ff717abb38fd1723f18e7b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{y = 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>We can also see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690ef55a607beaf2389d1ee102df817721bc2392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> doesn't work:\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690ef55a607beaf2389d1ee102df817721bc2392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf09bb6db966590d7cb146d78f0df45ff9314784.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 3 + 3y = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/7/2577c70d7adef584ac32fcef4b0cbd26e65f3054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(5 + y) = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must be an integer, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/8/d285a284c7a630163ce5a31e4a052b7f4a71d38f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 + y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" /> is an integer, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/6/cf661c4171aa4eafb8959e4d782cbae837173d16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(5 + y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" /> would have to be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This isn't the case here, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690ef55a607beaf2389d1ee102df817721bc2392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> doesn't work either.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1.5_.28Modular_Arithmetic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5_(Modular_Arithmetic)\">Solution 1.5 (Modular Arithmetic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_D&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5 (Modular Arithmetic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can follow the same steps as solution 1, to the point where we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/d/efd5af5222f3d671e7d292d33599ff82e2edf247.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x + 3y = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Like in solution 1, we can realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Using modular arithmetic, we see:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/8/f3841f6c32211800600d955e03ec8ea9add0ecb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x + 3y \\equiv 19 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"177\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca3a38a5f51b4c1609848e5677dc0bedc393437e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/7/d879f756843c334b1fc8dbcf9a4200d1c198e6a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x \\equiv 1 \\times 2 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/1/4c17b7798a15d7e2c1a7ed40c04eed46d6965ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more than a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, this can only occur when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/1/0b124361978352af059e12c33e0b92950ae1c850.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x = 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"57\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>Like in solution 1, we can just plug-in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2effc7979b1c93e59356b73253d75e2740b33105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/d/efd5af5222f3d671e7d292d33599ff82e2edf247.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5x + 3y = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" /> and eventually get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/9/cd92814176db02f14ff717abb38fd1723f18e7b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{y = 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018061946\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 347/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 302/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 13148/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.547      1 2018_CIMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\n100.00%    6.547      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37103:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018061946 and revision id 286425. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}